# Cleans up telemirror's orphaned temp files (videos and re-uploaded
# documents) from the shared /tmp. In normal operation the watermark/media
# filters' `finally` deletes them, and systemd units also get PrivateTmp=true
# (the namespace dies with the process). This cron job is a safety net for
# manual past_mode.py runs outside systemd, and for OOM crashes. The
# telemirror-tmp- prefix (set via tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(prefix=...) in
# _media.py / watermarkfilter.py) keeps this scoped to telemirror's own
# files — plain 'tmp*' would also match any other tool's default-named temp
# files sitting in the same shared /tmp on this host (e.g. postgresql).
# -type f keeps it scoped to regular files only.
19 * * * * root find /tmp -maxdepth 1 -type f -name 'telemirror-tmp-*' -mmin +180 -delete 2>/dev/null
